        "type": "text",
        "text": "Official statistics for the Faroe Islands from the StatBank of Statistics Faroe Islands (Hagstova Føroya). This server is not affiliated with or endorsed by Statistics Faroe Islands.\n\nTo answer a question with data:\n1. Call `search_tables` with short topic keywords. English (\"en\") search is the most reliable; Faroese (\"fo\") search matches whole words only. Results marked \"archived\" are discontinued tables; prefer current tables.\n2. Call `get_table_metadata` on the best table to see its variables and value codes. Use `valueFilter` to find a municipality or island by name.\n3. Call `query_table` with only the values you need. Use `latest` for recent periods.\n\nAlways cite the source line that each result ends with. If you change the data or calculate new figures, say so, for example \"Statistics Faroe Islands and own calculations\"."
      }
    ],
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hvussu nógv fiskur varð útfluttur í fjør?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "search_tables",
        "description": "Find tables by keywords in their titles. Returns table ids, titles and publish dates, best match first. Search with short topic words, for example \"unemployment municipalities\", not full questions.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "query": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 2,
              "description": "Keywords to search for."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of titles. Default \"fo\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "fo",
                "en"
              ]
            },
            "limit": {
              "description": "Maximum results. Default 10.",
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 50
            },
            "includeArchived": {
              "description": "Also list discontinued tables, for older periods. Default false.",
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "query"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "get_table_metadata",
        "description": "List the variables of a table and their value codes. Call this before query_table. Long value lists are shortened; use valueFilter to find specific values, for example a municipality name.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "tableId": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Table id exactly as search_tables returns it."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of labels. Default \"fo\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "fo",
                "en"
              ]
            },
            "valueFilter": {
              "description": "Show only values whose label contains this text, for example \"Ljubljana\".",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tableId"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "query_table",
        "description": "Get data from a table as CSV with readable labels. For each variable, give value codes from get_table_metadata, or \"latest\" for the most recent N periods. Results above 5000 cells, or too large for the context, are refused with advice on how to narrow the query.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
          "properties": {
            "tableId": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Table id exactly as search_tables returns it."
            },
            "lang": {
              "description": "Language of labels. Default \"fo\".",
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "fo",
                "en"
              ]
            },
            "selections": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "code": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Variable code from get_table_metadata."
                  },
                  "values": {
                    "description": "Value codes to include.",
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "latest": {
                    "description": "Include only the last N values. Use it for time variables, for example the latest 4 quarters.",
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "code"
                ]
              },
              "description": "One entry per variable to filter. Leave out variables you do not need."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tableId",
            "selections"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "tool_choice": {
      "type": "auto"
    }
